[SIZE="5"][B]UltGrantTargeting[/B][/SIZE]

[COLOR="DarkOrange"][B]This is a diagnostic/research addon, not intended for general use.[/B][/COLOR]

[B]Required dependency:[/B] [URL="https://www.esoui.com/downloads/info4024-LibGroupCombatStats.html"]LibGroupCombatStats[/URL]

LibGroupCombatStats has its own requirements that you'll also need to install:
[LIST]
[*][URL="https://www.esoui.com/downloads/info2528-LibCombat.html"]LibCombat[/URL]
[*][URL="https://www.esoui.com/downloads/info1337-LibGroupBroadcast.html"]LibGroupBroadcast[/URL]
[*][URL="https://www.esoui.com/downloads/info2275-LibDebugLogger.html"]LibDebugLogger[/URL]
[/LIST]

UltGrantTargeting is a testing tool designed to gather data about how ultimate-granting set effects select their targets. Specifically, it investigates:

[LIST]
[*]How do [B]Arkasis' Genius[/B], [B]Colovian Highlands General[/B], and [B]Cryptcannon Vestments[/B] choose which group members receive ultimate?
[*]Is target selection based on proximity, lowest ultimate, group index, or random?
[*]When a group member [I]cannot[/I] gain ultimate (e.g., during [B]Magma Armor[/B] or [B]Bone Goliath Transformation[/B]), does the set skip them and pick someone else, or does it waste a target slot on them?
[/LIST]

The addon logs every ultimate energize event (ACTION_RESULT_POWER_ENERGIZE with COMBAT_MECHANIC_FLAGS_ULTIMATE) along with a full group state snapshot — each member's ultimate level, position, distance from the caster, combat state, alive/dead/online status, and whether they're under an ability that blocks ultimate gain. All data is saved to SavedVariables for offline analysis.

[URL="https://github.com/Kickimanjaro/UltGrantTargeting"]Source on GitHub[/URL]

[COLOR="DarkOrange"][SIZE="4"]Slash Commands[/SIZE][/COLOR]

[LIST]
[*][B]/ugt status[/B] — Show current ult, group state, active ult-blocking abilities, LGCS connection, verbose/discovery mode, and session stats
[*][B]/ugt verbose[/B] — Toggle verbose mode (show events in chat; off by default)
[*][B]/ugt snapshot[/B] — Print a group state snapshot to chat (positions, ult, combat status)
[*][B]/ugt scan[/B] — Dump all buffs on self or group members, highlighting ult-blocking abilities
[*][B]/ugt discover[/B] — Toggle discovery mode (log all power energize events to find unknown ability IDs)
[*][B]/ugt note <text>[/B] — Insert an annotated snapshot into the log as a test boundary marker
[*][B]/ugt procs[/B] — Show recent tracked set proc events
[*][B]/ugt recent[/B] — Show all recent ultimate energize events
[*][B]/ugt limit[/B] — View or set savedvar size limits (sessions, procs, log entries)
[*][B]/ugt clear[/B] — Clear the current session log
[*][B]/ugt help[/B] — List all commands
[/LIST]

[COLOR="DarkOrange"][SIZE="4"]Data[/SIZE][/COLOR]

All events are saved to the [B]UltGrantTargeting[/B] saved variable file. Each tracked set proc includes:

[LIST]
[*]The triggering ability (source, target, ability ID, ult amount)
[*]Additional targets that received ult from the same proc (within a 150ms debounce window)
[*]A full group snapshot at the time of the proc (ult values, positions, combat/dead/online status, ult-blocking state)
[*]A human-readable summary cross-referencing targets against the snapshot (identifies blocked, dead, or skipped members)
[/LIST]

To keep the saved variable file from growing unbounded, all storage is capped with configurable limits:

[LIST]
[*][B]Sessions:[/B] max 10 retained (oldest pruned on login)
[*][B]Procs:[/B] max 500 per session (oldest removed when exceeded)
[*][B]Log entries:[/B] max 2000 per session (ring buffer — overwrites oldest entries in place, no table resizing)
[/LIST]

All three limits can be viewed and adjusted in-game with [B]/ugt limit[/B]. The current session can also be wiped at any time with [B]/ugt clear[/B].

You can then later review [B]UltGrantTargeting.lua[/B] in your SavedVariables folder.

[COLOR="DarkOrange"][SIZE="4"]Tracked Sets[/SIZE][/COLOR]

[LIST]
[*][B]Arkasis' Genius[/B] — ability ID 142660 (grants +44 ult to you and 3 group members on potion use)
[*][B]Colovian Highlands General[/B] — ability ID 202843 (grants +15 ult/stack to you and up to 5 group members within 28m on player kill)
[*][B]Cryptcannon Vestments[/B] (Crypt Transfer) — ability ID 195031 (consumes your ult and distributes it to nearby group members)
[/LIST]
